          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3339080">Gimli*/GeoJoce</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP212 Edmonton&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found this cap tonight with GJ and the geodawg on another quick jaunt.  GJ agreed to make the drive with me after a tiring day for both of us and thankfully this cap was another quick find.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A large hole, quite visible as we drove up to the site.  I managed to snap a couple of pics again.  We walked a circle around the 'island' before hopping back in the car and on for home.  Only one cap tonight but sure glad to grab another one before Monday.  TFTBC OFTH!  Wish I had gotten into seriously finding these just a bit earlier.  :)&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680208748">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP212 Edmonton 

In North Edmonton grabbing some BCPs before the end of the month. Easily found but difficult to read. Combination of cuts, scuffs and paint had obliterated some of the numbers. 

Thanks outforthehunt for another BCP. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
